    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98f81b30_25df1831",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T10:49:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure that I understand why we need all these pieces of state to know what to do with objects that have contents (buffers, textures, querysets). Won\u0027t we capture all the operations that may modify them, such that capturing their contents the first time that the `CaptureContext` sees them would be sufficient? This would handle the complexity mentioned here about the 2nd capture, as the CaptureContext should be reset for the second capture, and when `AddResource` is called, the object would be considered \"new\" for the capture and its contents captured.",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f0b4a7c_d23aa9b6",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T15:41:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Did you look at the tests? They don\u0027t pass without these. The tests should make it clear what they are for.\n\n\u003e Won\u0027t we capture all the operations that may modify them\n\nThere\u0027s nothing to capture with mapAsync. All we do is mark it as \"mNeedsCapture\" and the code automatically captures it **IF** it\u0027s used again.",
      "parentUuid": "98f81b30_25df1831",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b4d1b48_dba7ffd6",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T16:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[2]\n\nI did look at the tests (and I actually spent an hour reviewing this to try to understand why state was added). None of them do a map between two submits and as far as I can tell the current tests would pass with the suggested simplifications.\n\nIt makes sense that if we only track queue operations, then mapping wouldn\u0027t be visible in the trace. AFAIK it is the only non-queue operation that updates the contents of a resources, so WDYT of adding the data updates to the trace as a WriteBuffer in UnmapImpl instead? This way users will see the data uploads that they do and we avoid the need to track multiple additional booleans per recordable objects (that we have to statefully update in all the places in the backend that touch buffer/texture).",
      "parentUuid": "3f0b4a7c_d23aa9b6",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec36f420_a895ad3d",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 56,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T19:14:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think doing it unmapimpl is a distraction to the user. The buffer might not be used again even if they did update it. The current impl is \"on submit, upload all resources needed for the submit\".  The user can do map/unmap/map/unmap many times before submitting but we only need to capture once and only if the buffer is actually used.",
      "parentUuid": "0b4d1b48_dba7ffd6",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc84ac31_d5187a69",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T10:49:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need to special case the buffers being initialized or not? Is it an optimization used to not readback a bunch of zeroes? As a first step we could just readback the zeroes IMHO. But also in `Buffer::CaptureContentImpl` we can look at [`IsInitialized`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Buffer.h;drc\u003d44d2b5fba87c4b77729b3b52c9352f1e629ed114;l\u003d125) to know if the buffer is uninitialized (hence as-if filled with zeroes) or initialized in which case it has already been used and should contain non-zeroes (unless the only use was to read it, but then the application is doing useless work, so it\u0027s fine for the capture to do useless work).\n\nThis might remove the need for the calls to `MarkAsNeedCapture` when resources are written to.",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f686aa3_b8cb9aa3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T15:41:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why do we need to special case the buffers being initialized or not? Is it an optimization used to not readback a bunch of zeroes? \n\nIt\u0027s generic for RecordableObject. We don\u0027t want to read back empty render targets do we? They are large. Further, there\u0027s `clearBuffer` (as in fill with data, call clearBuffer, then capture. No need to capture the buffer\u0027s contents even though it\u0027s been initialized).",
      "parentUuid": "cc84ac31_d5187a69",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a27f7ff2_bee4a800",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/webgpu/RecordableObject.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 65,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-13T16:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For buffers, `clearBuffer` takes a range and a clear value so it\u0027s not the same as filling it with zeroes. For textures we can also query if they are initialized before doing a readback. A texture that\u0027s not initialized while used as a render target should be detectable in the WebGPU backend as backends are supposed to call [`LazyClearRenderPassAttachments`](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/CommandBuffer.h;drc\u003d62a9a00176f862e688fa47919ed6f19b59f77b5f;l\u003d94) themselves (so they need to know the initialized status).",
      "parentUuid": "1f686aa3_b8cb9aa3",
      "revId": "2f61752c7d75f9b588406cf301e79244127dc248",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
